<id/19/1994/#concept> a <http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/E55_Type>, skos:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "Mittens"@en ;
    skos:broader <id/grp/grp_woven_fabrics_apparel/#concept> ;
    skos:definition "MITTS, thin ladies' gloves without fingers, of silk, net or lace; men's warm wrappings for the hands made of cloth, worsted, &c., differing from gloves in having no separate divisions for the fingers. [P. L. Simmonds, The Commercial Dictionary of Trade Products (1892), scan p. 261]"@en ;
    skos:editorialNote "Curated classification (group=grp_woven_fabrics_apparel; processing_state=manufactured): Named textile/apparel article (woollens, moccasins, mittens, wrought inkle = linen tape per Simmonds 1892 s.v. INKLE, floorcloth) left in the residual bin. Layer-1 observations: 1 rows, 1807–1807. Series: CSP_Canadian_Exports_BlankSeries (inferred, series not printed) ×1. Units: Pairs ×1. Top routes: Quebec QC → Great Britain ×1."@en ;
    skos:inScheme <id/scheme/#resource> ;
    skos:notation "1994" ;
    skos:prefLabel "Mittens"@en ;
